<%# Shared form fields for creating and editing a commission rank. %>
<div class="field-row wide-first">
  <div class="field">
    <label>Rank name</label>
    <input type="text" name="name" required value="<%= p.name || '' %>" placeholder="Standard, Senior, Partner…">
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label>Seniority</label>
    <input type="number" name="rank_order" value="<%= p.rank_order || 0 %>">
    <div class="help">Higher is more senior. A promotion only ever moves an agent up this number.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="field">
  <label>Description <span class="muted small">(optional)</span></label>
  <input type="text" name="description" value="<%= p.description || '' %>"
         placeholder="For agents with six or more closed deals">
</div>

<fieldset>
  <legend>The basis</legend>
  <div class="field">
    <label>Deal value <span class="muted small">(optional)</span></label>
    <input type="number" step="0.01" min="0" name="deal_value"
           placeholder="<%= campaign.deal_value || 0 %> — inherited from the campaign"
           value="<%= (p.deal_value === null || p.deal_value === undefined) ? '' : p.deal_value %>">
    <div class="help">
      Leave blank to use the campaign's deal value
      (<strong><%= money(campaign.deal_value || 0, campaign.currency) %></strong>), which is
      almost always what you want. Fill it in only when this rank genuinely sells
      something of a different value. Percentages below calculate from whichever applies.
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="help mb-0">
    Paid in <strong><%= campaign.currency %></strong>, set on the campaign. One campaign, one
    currency — otherwise two ranks could disagree and the totals would quietly add them together.
  </p>
</fieldset>

<fieldset>
  <legend>Initial commission</legend>
  <div class="field-row">
    <div class="field mb-0">
      <label>Type</label>
      <select name="initial_type">
        <option value="percentage" <%= p.initial_type === 'percentage' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Percentage of deal value</option>
        <option value="fixed" <%= p.initial_type === 'fixed' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Fixed amount</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="field mb-0">
      <label>Value</label>
      <input type="number" step="0.01" min="0" name="initial_value" value="<%= p.initial_value || 0 %>">
    </div>
  </div>
</fieldset>

<fieldset>
  <legend>Recurring commission</legend>
  <div class="check">
    <input type="checkbox" id="rec-<%= p.id || 'new' %>" name="recurring_enabled" value="1" <%= p.recurring_enabled ? 'checked' : '' %>>
    <div><label for="rec-<%= p.id || 'new' %>">This rank earns a monthly recurring commission</label></div>
  </div>
  <div class="field-row three">
    <div class="field mb-0">
      <label>Type</label>
      <select name="recurring_type">
        <option value="percentage" <%= p.recurring_type === 'percentage' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Percentage</option>
        <option value="fixed" <%= p.recurring_type === 'fixed' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Fixed</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="field mb-0">
      <label>Value</label>
      <input type="number" step="0.01" min="0" name="recurring_value" value="<%= p.recurring_value || 0 %>">
    </div>
    <div class="field mb-0">
      <label>Months</label>
      <input type="number" min="1" max="120" name="recurring_months" value="<%= p.recurring_months || '' %>" placeholder="blank = while active">
    </div>
  </div>
</fieldset>

<fieldset>
  <legend>How an agent earns this rank</legend>
  <p class="help mt-0">
    Leave off and you promote people by hand. Switch it on and the nightly job moves
    anyone who qualifies up to this rank — and tells them. It never moves anyone down.
  </p>

  <div class="check">
    <input type="checkbox" id="auto-<%= p.id || 'new' %>" name="auto_promote" value="1"
           <%= p.auto_promote ? 'checked' : '' %>>
    <div><label for="auto-<%= p.id || 'new' %>">Promote agents automatically when they qualify</label></div>
  </div>

  <div class="field-row">
    <div class="field mb-0">
      <label>After this many closed deals</label>
      <input type="number" min="1" name="promote_after_deals"
             value="<%= p.promote_after_deals || '' %>" placeholder="e.g. 6">
    </div>
    <div class="field mb-0">
      <label>After earning this much</label>
      <input type="number" step="0.01" min="0" name="promote_after_amount"
             value="<%= p.promote_after_amount || '' %>"
             placeholder="e.g. 5000">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="help">
    Both are optional and both count only on this campaign. Set both and an agent must
    meet <em>both</em> before moving up. Set neither and automatic promotion stays off,
    because a rank with no requirement would promote everybody the first time it ran.
  </div>
</fieldset>

<div class="field-row three">
  <div class="field">
    <label>Payout day</label>
    <input type="number" min="1" max="28" name="payout_day" value="<%= p.payout_day || 15 %>">
    <div class="help">Day of the month, 1–28.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label>Status</label>
    <select name="status">
      <option value="active" <%= p.status === 'active' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Active</option>
      <option value="archived" <%= p.status === 'archived' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Archived</option>
    </select>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label>Default rank</label>
    <div class="check" style="margin:6px 0 0">
      <input type="checkbox" id="def-<%= p.id || 'new' %>" name="is_default" value="1" <%= p.is_default ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <div><label for="def-<%= p.id || 'new' %>">New joiners get this rank</label></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
